# Performance wiki markers

In `wiki/Performance.md` and `wiki/Performance-Profiling.md`:

- **🟢** marks the highest **sustainable** RPS among comparable products on that row.
- Put **🟢 only inside markdown table cells** (sustain columns).
- Do **not** use 🟢 in prose, notes, captions, or bullet lists (except the short legend that defines the marker).
- In narrative, say “leads” / “TWP leads” / “YARP leads” instead of “TWP 🟢”.

```markdown
<!-- ❌ BAD — prose -->
Early-response H1: TWP 🟢 (~1.25× YARP).

<!-- ✅ GOOD — prose -->
Early-response H1: TWP leads (~1.25× YARP).

<!-- ✅ GOOD — table cell -->
| … | 🟢 **7,099** | **7,531** | … |

<!-- ✅ GOOD — legend only -->
- 🟢 = highest sustainable RPS among products with a number on that row.
```
